course: dictionary
lesson: 2696
title: Difficult: one word, three meanings
level: primary-4
stars: 0
explain: The word difficult means hard to do, understand or deal with. Read the words around it to find which meaning fits. «Perseverance means keeping going when things are difficult.» Here difficult means hard to get through, like a tough time you have to keep going through.
explain: Difficult can also mean full of problems or worries. «"The terrible twos" means the difficult stage of a toddler around age two.» Nobody is saying the toddler is hard to do. The stage itself is full of problems.
explain: Ask yourself what the word describes: a task, a time, or a person. «In a tight crowd a person can be squeezed so hard that breathing becomes difficult.» Breathing is the hard thing to do here. Try your meaning in the sentence to check it still makes sense.
fact: Difficult is an adjective, and its comparison is more difficult, most difficult.
fact: «Difficult» means hard to do, understand or deal with, needing a lot of effort or skill.
fact: «Difficult» can mean full of problems or worries, as in «a difficult time».
fact: «Difficult» can describe a person who is not easy to please or get on with.
fact: Useful phrases: «find it difficult to», «make life difficult», «a difficult decision».
exercise: «Perseverance means keeping going when things are difficult.» What does difficult mean here? | Easy and fun | *Hard to get through | Full of bright colours | Very loud
exercise: Dad says, «That was a difficult day at work.» What does difficult mean? | Hard to hear | Easy to please | Very quick | *Full of problems or worries
exercise: «He is so difficult that nobody wants to sit next to him.» What does difficult mean? | Easy to please, always smiling | *Not easy to get on with | Full of colour | Hard to say aloud
test: «I find it difficult to sleep when the room is hot.» What does difficult mean here? | *Hard to do or get through | Very bright | Full of colour
test: What does the phrase «make life difficult» mean? | *Cause trouble and problems | Live in a big house | Make life easy and calm | Go to bed early
exam: «My little brother is difficult at bedtime, always refusing to sleep.» Which meaning of difficult is used? | *Not easy to please or get on with | Full of colour | Hard to lift | Very bright
